<title>CANADA: Canada's Prairies to see rain west, sun east.</title>
<headline>Canada's Prairies to see rain west, sun east.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies on Wedneday were forecast to see some rain in the west but mainly sunny skies, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Alberta should see rain in the west central and northern regions, sun elsewhere and highs of 24 to 29 Celsius.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should see sunny skies with late day showers in the west and highs of 28 to 34 Celsius.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see sunny skies with highs of 27 to 30 Celsius.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
